{
  "index": 52,
  "text": "The real-world effectiveness of camrelizumab in our advanced esophageal cancer patients is generally consistent with pivotal camrelizumab trials [8\u201311] (Supplementary Table 8), with nivolizumab in heavily pretreated advanced ESCC [15], and better than pembrolizumab in heavily pretreated esophageal adenocarcinoma or squamous cell carcinoma [16], although observational and trial results are not directly comparable [17, 18]. Unlike predefined trial populations, our study included fragile patients aged \u2265 75 years (13.3%) and those with an ECOG performance status of \u2265 2 (6.7%) who would not have met trial eligibility criteria. Unlike highly protocolized trial care, real-world practice involves varying treatment patterns and inconsistent timing and criteria for radiological response assessment, which may have affected outcomes, especially ORR and PFS. Nevertheless, OS, a robust endpoint, was consistent with that of pivotal trials, supporting the effectiveness of camrelizumab in real-world patients.",
